/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  THE INTERNAL STATE OF ONE UNIT, inside the state view that
  holds its streams.  A state directory is a RESTARTABLE
  SNAPSHOT: the streams are the boundary, this is what the
  equipment holds between them.  One file per unit, one block
  per kind of field (stageProfile, axialProfile,
  sizeDistribution, swingTable), filed under `internalStates/`
  so a unit and a stream sharing a name can never collide.

  In `converged/` this file is REGENERATED WHOLE on every run
  together with the streams beside it.  Do not edit it there --
  an edit is destroyed by the next run without a word.

  COPY it into the case's `0/internalStates/` at the
  same address to DECLARE it as the interior the next
  run starts from -- this unit reads stageProfile.  A
  declared profile that does not satisfy the balances
  is a SEED, not an answer.

  It is a PROJECTION of the profile this unit publishes through
  `UnitOperation::profile()` -- the same record the result JSON
  carries under `profiles` and `profile.csv` carries in the
  reports.  Nothing here was computed for this file.

  Internal state is a field over a coordinate of the equipment
  (position, stage, particle size) or its inventory (loadings
  per component); a construction over a parameter sweep
  (van Heerden, Merkel) is an analysis and stays in the reports.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

